 A biopsy ruled out squamous cell carcinoma. On December 9, 2019, he underwent surgical debridement of the unviable tissues and reconstruction using a right ALT flap based on two musculocutaneous perforators, extended laterally to the vastus lateralis muscle to include a segment of fascia lata and elevated as a composite flap (
Fig. 2
).

 A pediatric neurologist examined the patient and found no abnormal findings; the patient did not have leg weakness or sensory loss. However, MRI of the brain and the spinal cord was done and revealed syringohydromyelia extending from thoracic spine (Th5) to conus medullaris with 6 to 7 mm in diameter (
Fig. 1
).

